# cstacks Job Script for use on SI Hydra 

Script Name: hydra_cstacks.qsub

DESCRIPTION
-----------
This script runs the Stacks program `cstacks` to build a catalog of loci from all samples listed in a population map (popmap) file. 
The catalog serves as the reference database used in downstream Stacks analyses.

The script is designed to run on a Sun Grid Engine (SGE) cluster and uses multiple CPU threads.

WORKFLOW POSITION
-----------------
This script is run after all samples have been processed with `ustacks`.

```
process_radtags
    ↓
ustacks ← hydra_uStacks_array.qsub
    ↓
cstacks *← this script, hydra_cStacks.qsub
    ↓
sstacks ← hydra_sStacks_array.qsub
    ↓
tsv2bam
    ↓
gstacks
    ↓
populations
```

IMPORTANT NOTE
--------------
Unlike `ustacks` and `sstacks`, `cstacks` can NOT be run as an array job.

`cstacks` builds a single catalog using information from all samples in the dataset. 

REQUIREMENTS
------------
Software:
    - Stacks v2.66 or later
    - Sun Grid Engine (SGE)

Module loaded:

    module load bioinformatics/stacks/2.66

INPUT FILES
-----------
1. Stacks Working Directory

The directory specified with the `-P` option must contain the output files generated by `ustacks`.

Example files:

    sample01.tags.tsv.gz
    sample01.snps.tsv.gz
    sample01.alleles.tsv.gz

    sample02.tags.tsv.gz
    sample02.snps.tsv.gz
    sample02.alleles.tsv.gz

    ...

2. Population Map File (Popmap)

The file specified with the `-M` option contains sample IDs and population assignments.

Example:

    sample01 population1
    sample02 population1
    sample03 population2
    sample04 population2

Sample names in the popmap must exactly match the sample names present in the Stacks output files.

RESOURCE REQUESTS
-----------------
The script requests:

    32 CPU cores
    Queue: mThC.q
    Reserved memory: 256 GB
    h_data: 8 GB
    h_vmem: 6 GB

These values may need to be adjusted depending on the size of the dataset and cluster policies.

SCRIPT CONFIGURATION
--------------------
Modify the cstacks command before submitting the job:

    cstacks \
        -n 6 \
        -p "${NSLOTS}" \
        -P /Path/to/stacks/working/directory \
        -M /Path/to/stacks/sample/population/file/popmap.txt

Example:

    cstacks \
        -n 6 \
        -p "${NSLOTS}" \
        -P /data/project/stacks \
        -M /data/project/popmap.txt

PARAMETER DESCRIPTIONS
----------------------
-n 6
    Number of mismatches allowed between loci when constructing the catalog.

-p "${NSLOTS}"
    Number of CPU threads allocated by SGE.

-P
    Path to the Stacks working directory containing the results generated by `ustacks`.

-M
    Path to the population map file.

JOB SUBMISSION
--------------
Submit the job using:

```
    qsub hydra_cstacks.qsub
````

OUTPUT FILES
------------
Successful execution generates catalog files in the specified Stacks working directory.

Typical outputs include:

    catalog.tags.tsv.gz
    catalog.snps.tsv.gz
    catalog.alleles.tsv.gz

These files are required for downstream analyses, particularly `sstacks`.

LOG FILE
--------
Job output is written to:

    cStacks.log

The log contains:

    - Job start time
    - Host information
    - Resource allocation
    - cstacks progress messages
    - Error messages
    - Job completion information

TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
No catalog files created

    Verify that:
    - All ustacks jobs completed successfully.
    - The Stacks directory contains the expected sample files.
    - The popmap file is formatted correctly.

Popmap not found

    Check the path:

        ls -l /path/to/popmap.txt

Samples missing from catalog

    Confirm that sample names in the popmap exactly match the sample names generated by ustacks.

Memory errors

    Increase memory requests as needed based on dataset size and cluster resources.

NOTES
-----
- Run `ustacks` on all samples before running `cstacks`.
- `cstacks` produces a single catalog for the entire project.
- The generated catalog is required before running `sstacks`.


